res-rahul-gandhi-amid-sir-stir-criticises-police-brutality/articleshow/134944141.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T19:15:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134944319,imgsize-125190.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Starlink row: Govt set to examine satellite internet, says parliamentary panel chief Nishikant Dubey]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/starlink-row-govt-set-to-examine-satellite-internet-says-parliamentary-panel-chief-nishikant-dubey/articleshow/134943629.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134943629.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Indian parliamentary panel will soon discuss satellite internet services following Elon Musk's allegations about market access and opposition. Musk claims powerful business interests are obstructing Starlink's entry into India while urging competition. The government has rejected these allegations, stating security and regulatory requirements are crucial. BJP MP Nishikant Dubey emphasized security agencies' concerns regarding Starlink's operations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/starlink-row-govt-set-to-examine-satellite-internet-says-parliamentary-panel-chief-nishikant-dubey/articleshow/134943629.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/starlink-row-govt-set-to-examine-satellite-internet-says-parliamentary-panel-chief-nishikant-dubey/articleshow/134943629.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T18:56:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134943989,imgsize-55326.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening news wrap: Woman, lover get death sentence in Blue Drum murder case; US ends automatic work permit extensions &amp; more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-woman-lover-get-death-sentence-in-blue-drum-murder-case-us-ends-automatic-work-permit-extensions-more/articleshow/134943291.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134943291.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A Meerut court sentenced Muskan Rastogi and Sahil Shukla to death for murdering Saurabh Rajput, which occurred in March 2025. The court issued the verdict following a trial that included testimony from 22 prosecution witnesses. Meanwhile, the US announced the end of automatic work permit extensions for H-4 visa holders, impacting many Indian spouses.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-woman-lover-get-death-sentence-in-blue-drum-murder-case-us-ends-automatic-work-permit-extensions-more/articleshow/134943291.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-woman-lover-get-death-sentence-in-blue-drum-murder-case-us-ends-automatic-work-permit-extensions-more/articleshow/134943291.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T18:43:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134943741,imgsize-759789.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi protests: Pakistan-linked handles under probe for fake claims of police firing]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-protests-pakistan-linked-handle-under-probe-for-fake-claims-of-police-firing/articleshow/134943082.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134943082.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-protests-pakistan-linked-handle-under-probe-for-fake-claims-of-police-firing/articleshow/134943082.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-protests-pakistan-linked-handle-under-probe-for-fake-claims-of-police-firing/articleshow/134943082.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T18:16:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134943206,imgsize-221208.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi protest: Journalists slapped with SC/ST Act for casteist slur against ACP on duty]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-protest-journalists-slapped-with-sc/st-act-for-casteist-slur-against-acp-on-duty/articleshow/134941545.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134941545.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The FIR was registered on October 13 at Parliament Street Police Station on the complaint of ACP Vivek Bhagat, who is posted in the Connaught Place subdivision. Journalist Rosy, Gajendra Singh, who is associated with a news portal, and an unidentified person have been named as accused. The case has been registered under provisions of the Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-protest-journalists-slapped-with-sc/st-act-for-casteist-slur-against-acp-on-duty/articleshow/134941545.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-protest-journalists-slapped-with-sc/st-act-for-casteist-slur-against-acp-on-duty/articleshow/134941545.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T17:42:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134942544,imgsize-195738.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Advancing our Strategic Partnership’: EAM Jaishankar meets Canadian counterpart Anita Anand as India, Canada push to reset ties]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advancing-our-strategic-partnership-eam-jaishankar-meets-canadian-counterpart-anita-anand-as-india-canada-push-to-reset-ties/articleshow/134940846.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134940846.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar and Canadian Foreign Minister Anita Anand met to enhance bilateral relations. They discussed trade, investment, energy, defense, and education, aiming to advance the Strategic Partnership. Prime Ministers Modi and Carney also spoke to build momentum towards the India-Canada Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement. Canadian corporate delegation is exploring joint ventures in multiple sectors during their visit.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advancing-our-strategic-partnership-eam-jaishankar-meets-canadian-counterpart-anita-anand-as-india-canada-push-to-reset-ties/articleshow/134940846.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advancing-our-strategic-partnership-eam-jaishankar-meets-canadian-counterpart-anita-anand-as-india-canada-push-to-reset-ties/articleshow/134940846.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T17:33:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134942052,imgsize-177428.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Four Indians still in ICU': MEA condemns attack on Saudi airport, oil facilities]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/four-indians-still-in-icu-mea-condemns-attack-on-saudi-airport-oil-facilities/articleshow/134942244.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134942244.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/four-indians-still-in-icu-mea-condemns-attack-on-saudi-airport-oil-facilities/articleshow/134942244.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/four-indians-still-in-icu-mea-condemns-attack-on-saudi-airport-oil-facilities/articleshow/134942244.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T17:32:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134942319,imgsize-95772.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Your Didi is with you - today and forever!' Mamata Banerjee to detained CJP activists]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/your-didi-is-with-you-today-and-forever-mamata-banerjee-to-detained-cjp-activists/articleshow/134939329.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134939329.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a message posted on X on Wednesday, Banerjee condemned the arrests of Ashutosh Ranka and Saurav Das, who were sent to judicial custody, and assured young people of her support. “Your Didi is with you - today and forever!” she wrote. The arrests came amid opposition protests in Delhi over alleged electoral irregularities and demands for the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner (CEC) Gyanesh Kumar.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/your-didi-is-with-you-today-and-forever-mamata-banerjee-to-detained-cjp-activists/articleshow/134939329.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/your-didi-is-with-you-today-and-forever-mamata-banerjee-to-detained-cjp-activists/articleshow/134939329.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T16:48:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134940824,imgsize-62234.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Why are you ruining nation?' CJP's Abhijeet Dipke heckled with 'CIA agent' remark at Delhi airport]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/why-are-you-ruining-nation-cjps-abhijeet-dipke-heckled-with-cia-agent-remark-at-delhi-airport/articleshow/134939956.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134939956.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Dipke landed in Delhi a day after his party's co-convenors, Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka, surreptitiously climbed a gate at the prohibited area of Jantar Mantar to protest against Chief Election Commissioner (CEC)  Gyanesh Kumar and the government, which has denotified Jantar Mantar as a designated protest site. Later, Das and Ranka were sent to 5-day judicial custody on the order of Delhi's special executive magistrate court.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/why-are-you-ruining-nation-cjps-abhijeet-dipke-heckled-with-cia-agent-remark-at-delhi-airport/articleshow/134939956.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/why-are-you-ruining-nation-cjps-abhijeet-dipke-heckled-with-cia-agent-remark-at-delhi-airport/articleshow/134939956.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T16:39:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134940599,imgsize-101671.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hijack code 7500 appeared, pilots said all normal: The mystery behind Air India's Frankfurt-Delhi flight scare]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hijack-code-7500-appeared-pilots-said-all-normal-the-mystery-behind-air-indias-frankfurt-delhi-flight-scare/articleshow/134938930.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134938930.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hijack-code-7500-appeared-pilots-said-all-normal-the-mystery-behind-air-indias-frankfurt-delhi-flight-scare/articleshow/134938930.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hijack-code-7500-appeared-pilots-said-all-normal-the-mystery-behind-air-indias-frankfurt-delhi-flight-scare/articleshow/134938930.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T16:05:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Saurabh Sinha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134939294,imgsize-105108.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India seeks Indo-Pacific where all countries make their own choices, protect their interests: Rajnath Singh]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-seeks-indo-pacific-where-all-countries-make-their-own-choices-protect-their-interests-rajnath-singh/articleshow/134939110.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134939110.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rajnath Singh emphasised that India’s Act East policy and the vision of SAGAR (Security and Growth for All in the Region) and MAHASAGAR (Mutual and Holistic Advancement for Security and Growth Across Regions) advocate for an open and multipolar cooperation, and the nation aligns them through ASEAN-led mechanisms that are central to its Indo-Pacific vision.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-seeks-indo-pacific-wher